# 11FTC Ticketing Management System — Context Diagram (DFD Level 0)
# Paste into https://play.d2lang.com/  |  Layout engine: elk
# Yourdon/DeMarco notation: circle = process, rectangle = external entity.

direction: right

title: |md
  # Data Flow Diagram — Level 0 (Context)
| {near: top-center; shape: text; style.font-size: 26}

staff: "IT Staff\n[external entity]" {
  shape: rectangle
  style.fill: "#0b3d91"
  style.font-color: "#ffffff"
}

admin: "IT Administrator\n[external entity]" {
  shape: rectangle
  style.fill: "#0b3d91"
  style.font-color: "#ffffff"
}

employee: "Employee\n[external entity]" {
  shape: rectangle
  style.fill: "#0b3d91"
  style.font-color: "#ffffff"
}

sys: "0\n11FTC Ticketing\nManagement System" {
  shape: circle
  style.fill: "#1f6feb"
  style.font-color: "#ffffff"
  width: 220
  height: 220
}

sheets: "Google Sheets\nIT Tracker\n[external entity]" {
  shape: rectangle
  style.fill: "#8b949e"
  style.font-color: "#ffffff"
}

idp: "Google Workspace SSO\n[external entity]" {
  shape: rectangle
  style.fill: "#8b949e"
  style.font-color: "#ffffff"
}

# --- data flows ---
employee -> staff: "IT concern\n(verbal — outside system boundary)" {style.stroke-dash: 3; style.font-size: 11}

staff -> sys: "ticket details, employee name,\ndepartment, main issue, concern,\nstatus updates, remarks"
sys -> staff: "ticket no., ticket list,\nticket history, dashboard"

admin -> sys: "employee records, user records,\nlookup values, sync configuration,\nvoid requests"
sys -> admin: "reports, dashboard metrics,\naudit trail, sync status"

sys -> sheets: "ticket rows\n(Date, Ticket No, Employee, Department,\nMain Issue, Concern, Assigned To,\nStatus, Remarks)"
sheets -> sys: "acknowledgement / API errors\n— NO ticket data returns" {style.stroke-dash: 3; style.stroke: "#d1242f"}

sys -> idp: "credentials"
idp -> sys: "identity assertion"

staff -> sheets: "reads newest-first view" {style.stroke-dash: 3}

note: |md
  **Reading this diagram**

  - **The Google Sheets flow is deliberately one-way.** The only return arrow
    carries acknowledgements and errors — never ticket data. This is FR-22, and it
    is the single most important constraint on the diagram: the moment data flows
    back, you own a conflict-resolution problem the SRS has no rule for.
  - **Employee sits outside the boundary.** They have no login and exchange no data
    with the system. The concern reaches the system only after IT Staff encodes it.
    The dashed arrow is context, not a system flow.
  - IT Staff also *reads* the sheet directly (dashed) — this is a human reading a
    Google tab, not a system interface, but it is why FR-25 exists.
| {near: bottom-center; shape: text}
